  "schema_version": 1,
  "_comment": "URLs must be immutable (dated release tags, versioned files) so the sha256 pins stay valid. Never point at 'latest' rolling URLs — the hash breaks on the next upstream push. exiftool is pinned via SourceForge because exiftool.org deletes old versions. ffmpeg MUST use a MONTH-END BtbN autobuild tag (autobuild-YYYY-MM-<last day of month>-HH-MM): BtbN keeps daily autobuilds for only ~2 weeks but retains the month-end build for 2+ years, so a mid-month pin 404s the release build a fortnight later (it did, on 2026-07-25). Note the archives are not byte-reproducible — the same filename and git rev rebuilt on another day hashes differently, so re-pin url AND sha256 together. To bump a dependency: update url+version, run fetch-bundled-deps with -Mode update to print the new hashes, paste them in, re-run with verify. macOS ffmpeg/ffprobe come from ffmpeg.martin-riedl.de's per-build directories (download/macos/<arch>/<buildid>_<version>/), which are immutable and keep history; evermeet.cx was dropped on 2026-10-16 because it rate-limits CI (HTTP 429 on the second download, and the macOS jobs fetch concurrently).",
